From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] RelicOS's own game-controller mappings over SDL's (RelicOS)

Observed on the device (M22 build 27): the Xbox pad (model 1708,
firmware 5.x) announces one of two product ids from one classic
Bluetooth connection to the next, 02fd or 02e0, with the same evdev
device behind both, and SDL's table maps 02e0 as the LE report layout.
The ES took that map at face value, wrote it to es_input.cfg, and the
pad was unplayable: select on the left shoulder, the right trigger read
as the right stick held up.

After SDL_INIT_JOYSTICK the ES loads /usr/share/relicos/
gamecontrollerdb.txt, RelicOS's mappings in SDL's own format; a mapping
added later wins over the built-in table for its GUID.
---
diff -ruN a/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp b/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp
--- a/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp	2026-09-14 14:30:59.598893087 -0300
+++ b/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp	2026-09-14 14:30:59.619729893 -0300
@@ -364,6 +364,19 @@
 	SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_GAMECONTROLLER_USE_BUTTON_LABELS, "0");
 #endif
 	SDL_InitSubSystem(SDL_INIT_JOYSTICK);
+#ifdef RELICOS
+	// RelicOS's own game-controller mappings, over SDL's table: a pad SDL
+	// maps wrong (the Xbox pad under its 02e0 identity, build 27) gets
+	// its right map here, on the rootfs, without touching SDL.
+	{
+		const char* relicosDb = "/usr/share/relicos/gamecontrollerdb.txt";
+		int added = SDL_GameControllerAddMappingsFromFile(relicosDb);
+		if (added >= 0)
+			LOG(LogInfo) << "InputManager: " << added << " mapping(s) from " << relicosDb;
+		else
+			LOG(LogWarning) << "InputManager: " << relicosDb << ": " << SDL_GetError();
+	}
+#endif
 
 	mJoysticksLock.lock();
 
